From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:09:57 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-media: decoder mode: take H.264 as well

Decoder mode (q11-041) offered one bitstream, HEVC, decoded by
rpi-hevc-dec through libavcodec's v4l2request hwaccel. The Raspberry
Pi 5 has no H.264 block, so the guest decoded H.264 itself: DomA's
Android software decoder on two vCPUs played 1080p60 at 35.4 fps.
DomD's libavcodec decodes the same stream at 95 fps on one thread.

decoder= now names the bitstreams the device offers: "hevc", "h264"
or both, joined by '+' (',' separates -device options), in any order.
ENUM_FMT on OUTPUT lists them HEVC first, and a session starts with
the first. S_FMT(OUTPUT) with another one opens libavcodec again for
it, and answers EBUSY while OUTPUT has buffers or either queue
streams; TRY_FMT changes nothing. H.264 is decoded in software, with
no hwaccel tried; HEVC keeps its path.

A frame libavcodec cannot decode (AVERROR_INVALIDDATA) is now that
frame lost: it used to end the session with EIO. Should a switch fail
to open either codec, avctx stays NULL: libavcodec is then called
only through dec_av_send, dec_av_receive and dec_av_flush, which
answer ENODEV or do nothing, and an S_FMT to that same codec tries to
open it again. The card name drops "HEVC".

Measured on the Raspberry Pi 5 8GB (2026-10-16, AOSP's codec tool
with -T; DomA's v4l2_codec2 picks c2.v4l2.avc.decoder before
c2.android.avc): H.264 1080p60 at 47.7 and 47.9 fps with the main loop
at 98 to 102% of a core, 720p60 at 61.1 and 61.2 fps. The frame goes
through swscale to RGBA and glTexSubImage2D on the main loop; the next
two patches take that off the CPU and the loop.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
